ly on the way out  the new york times has reported that he  is currently working on an exit package  now  hogwarts legacy fans will certainly  recognize the name jason keller because  it was just a few short weeks ago  that he tweeted out four pieces of  concept art and we discussed those here  on the channel  so that really just goes to show you how  fast things can change i mean he was  just tweeting out pictures for hogwarts  legacy hyping up the game talking about  how excited they were  and now today he appears to be on the  way out  now i mentioned that this was not  official yet and that's because this is  all still subject to regulatory approval  and  also approval from shareholders so it's  not 100 official  anytime there are big deals like this  with major major businesses  there are certain procedures these  companies have to follow and then  ultimately the government has to okay it  in fact some of you may remember nearly  a decade ago when at t announced their  plans to buy t-mobile  but this eventually hit a snag during  the regulatory process and it never  ended up happening  all that being said at the time of this  video recording both at t  and discovery have agreed to the deal  and are moving forward with this plan  so barring any snags there the merger is  expected to become official  sometime in 2022. on a broad scale the  core focus for this merger appears to be  an effort for dw to compete  with streaming giants like netflix and  disney plus as brian stelter of cnn put  it the move will quote  combine two treasure troves of content  including the hbo max  and discovery plus streaming services  close quote you see discovery owns  channels like tlc the food network  hgtv and plenty more warner media of  course owns  their fair share of major ips as well  such as dc comics  hbo cnn tnt and of course  harry potter at least a portion of harry  potter anyway as for how it seems right  now it would appear that  all of those ips will be under the new  