y potter  ip  of course remains with our new company  dw now whatever company avalanche  maybe sold to and then the new dw  company i think they would be able to  work something out to at least  finish the game you would expect that  when they put this much time and effort  into it it's  hopefully again close to the finish line  but here's where the curveball  comes in what about post launch support  what about any possible  dlc down the road my opinion today and  it is just that guys it is an opinion  this is an ever evolving situation  things have changed quite rapidly  already so this could all change by the  time this video gets out  but my opinion right now if i had to  guess is that hogwarts legacy will  end up releasing in 2022 but i do worry  about  two things number one avalanche's future  and number two post launch support for  the game  it certainly seemed like avalanche was  planning something really big here i  mean they had all these new hires  including a community manager i think  this was going to be a game with support  for quite some time  now if i had to lay out what i think  would be a best case scenario here  i think it would be for avalanche to  actually stay with wbie  which means they would move to the new  dw company and hopefully that new dw  leadership will just say hey  we like what you guys are doing just  keep doing what you're working on  they'll get to continue on their current  projects their current goals and maybe  even give some post-launch support  as well now this certainly is not going  to be the last  video that i make on this undoubtedly  this is going to come up again and again  so i want to hear from you guys in the  comments below  what questions do you all have about  this i still have so many questions as  well  in a deal this massive there are just so  many moving parts these changes won't be  able to happen overnight but you can  rest assured changes  will be coming guys they will be coming  to wb  avalanche and hones